Chapter 14: Working with Dimensions in Oracle FCCS
Source: Oracle Fusion Cloud EPM – Administering Financial Consolidation and Close (September 2026) | Chapter 14, 94 pages

Chapter 14 is one of the most important chapters for understanding FCCS application configuration. It explains the dimensions, hierarchies, member properties, accounts, entities, currencies, scenarios, and metadata used in consolidation.

For a four-year-experience FCCS interview, I recommend studying this chapter in detail.
1. What is a Dimension in FCCS?

A dimension organizes financial information into a particular category. 
Each dimension contains members arranged in hierarchies.

According to Oracle, FCCS provides predefined dimensions to support consolidation, translation, eliminations, and adjustments.



Oracle explains that the system creates only the dimensions required for the features enabled in the application.

Important: Default dimension properties cannot be changed because they are used in seeded calculations. EPM-INFORMATION-DEVELOPMENT-TEAM-E93973-628A1C2A_copy (1)(1).pdf

