Oracle FCCS – All Predefined Dimensions Explained with Real-Time Examples
In Oracle FCCS (Financial Consolidation and Close), predefined dimensions are dimensions provided by Oracle when an FCCS application is created.

They help organize financial data, perform calculations, translate currencies, consolidate subsidiaries, eliminate intercompany transactions, and generate financial statements.

We will understand each dimension using our ABC Global Group implementation project.
1. List of predefined dimensions in FCCS
FCCS has 11 core predefined dimensions, plus Multi-GAAP when that feature is enabled.
#	Dimension	Purpose	Example
1	Account	What financial account?	Cash, Revenue
2	Entity	Which company?	ABC India
3	Scenario	What type of data?	Actual, Budget
4	Year	Which financial year?	FY2026
5	Period	Which financial period?	January
6	View	How is data viewed?	Periodic, YTD
7	Currency	Which currency?	INR, USD
8	Consolidation	Which consolidation stage?	Entity Input, Contribution
9	Data Source	Where did the data originate?	Data Input, Journals
10	Movement	How did the balance change?	Opening Balance, Movements
11	Intercompany	Which related company?	ICP_ABC_USA
12	Multi-GAAP	Which accounting basis?	IFRS, Local GAAP

Important: Oracle supplies the dimensions and their required structures. You configure permitted members and properties within those dimensions. Some dimensions are primarily system-controlled, and optional dimensions or features depend on application configuration.

