FCCS Dimensions Quiz

Which dimension identifies the company to which financial data belongs?

A. Account

B. Entity

C. Scenario

D. Movement

 PreviousNext 

Interview-ready summary
A strong answer for a four-year FCCS consultant is:
Oracle FCCS provides predefined dimensions such as Account, Entity, Scenario, Year, Period, View, Currency, Consolidation, Data Source, Movement, and Intercompany, with Multi-GAAP available when enabled. These dimensions organize financial data and support translation, consolidation, eliminations, and reporting. Each financial value is stored at a specific intersection of dimension members, and member properties determine how that data is processed.

Most important for practical implementation: Account, Entity, Movement, Consolidation, Currency, Data Source, and Intercompany. Understanding how these seven dimensions interact will help you troubleshoot many real-world FCCS consolidation issues.
